{'name': 'Pearl Social Santa Barbara', 'address': '131 Anacapa St, Ste B', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Cocktail Bars, American (Traditional), Restaurants, Nightlife', 'hours': {'Monday': '17:0-22:0', 'Tuesday': '17:0-19:0', 'Thursday': '17:0-20:0', 'Friday': '17:0-0:0', 'Saturday': '17:30-0:0', 'Sunday': '17:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': True}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': True, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 20:19:14', 'review_text': "After a fun tour of the SB Funk Zone, and a delicious meal at The Lark, we all ventured next door to Pearl Social and were happily seated in their lounge are. Such an enchanting space, and perfect for socializing amongst the beautiful people of Santa Barbara.

Thank you Shannon and Alberto for taking such good care of us all. Shannon's drink recommendations were spot-on for all of us. 

Definitely our new favorite chill and cocktail place in the Funk Zone. And thoroughly enjoyed the fun music selections."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-09 00:58:46', 'review_text': 'Such a fun idea. We really hope they do another. It was a great way to celebrate New Years Day!'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-03 03:51:21', 'review_text': "we stumbled upon this on christmas eve and the vibes were PERFECT!!! super decked out pop up which was great, next christmas go check it out!! the bartenders were so fun and friendly, only reason not giving a 5 is because all the drinks were definitely on the super sweet side (which is fine for those who like it and it's christmas themed anyway so why not indulge?) but not everyone likes that sweet an some of us ending up getting just a beer (guess who) but so so fun!!"}]}

{'name': 'JJ’s Diner', 'address': '413 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Diners, Restaurants, Breakfast & Brunch', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '7:30-13:30', 'Wednesday': '7:30-13:30', 'Thursday': '7:30-13:30', 'Friday': '7:30-13:30', 'Saturday': '7:30-14:0', 'Sunday': '8:0-14:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': False, 'street': False, 'lot': True, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'divey': None, 'hipster': None, 'casual': None, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': None, 'intimate': None, 'romantic': None, 'classy': False, 'upscale': None}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-30 20:27:18', 'review_text': 'My husband and I were looking for a breakfast place while staying in Santa Barbara. We walked by this place and decided to try it out. First we were greeted with kind smiles and did not have to wait to be seated. Michael was our server and he was so so so kind! We ordered the Chile Verde Omelette and Eggs with Bacon. We received our food fast! The food was great, the service was amazing, and the environment was great!

Give this place a try!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-29 01:04:47', 'review_text': 'Great breakfast and service. Highly recommend. Staff even took care of noisy transients as they came on by - thank goodness !'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-28 19:02:22', 'review_text': "The wait to be seated was short despite the long line, they work quickly to get your food in front of you. The Customer service at this place is awesome and deserves 5 stars by itself. They are very friendly, prompt, and kept our coffees filled. If you notice the other reviews where Karens were complaining about bad service, were leaving reviews around when covid peaked so don't pay attention to those. I assure you the service is great.

The food is not bad, however it is basic, and safe. Don't get me wrong,  the food tasted fine, it's just that they play it safe which I guess is a good thing so that Karens in SB (There are plenty in this town) don't complain."}]}

{'name': 'El Taco Tequila Taqueria', 'address': '14 E Cota St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Mexican', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': True, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2013-12-06 03:03:14', 'review_text': "On Thursday night I went to this place after a concert. A few friends and I wanted a bite and a drink. We ordered with a young woman who quickly told us they did not accommodate gluten free customers, even if you wanted a taco or tostada without the bread. Fine. I'll work around that I understand. We waited 20 minutes for our food, granted there was only one guy in the kitchen. We finally got our tacos and were missing one chicken taco and our guacamole. We ask the chef for the rest of our order and he says they are closing the kitchen. I go to the woman and tell her that we didn't get all our food and she tells me I'm lying. I point to the plates on our table to show her we didn't. I ask for our money back and she declines. We end up getting into a fight about one chicken taco and guac. 

I have worked in restaurants before and I would never scold a customer over a $3 taco. I even offed to pay for it and she wouldn't let me. Really terrible customer service. The chef did make us some guac bc I think he felt bad that we were hungry and upset. By that point we had eaten what we were served and didn't have anything to put it on.

That being said the food we get was yummy. Too bad our experience ended on such a bad note."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2013-03-28 15:50:04', 'review_text': "We both got food poisoning here - that lasted a whole day. We narrowed it down to either the chips & salsa, the queso app, or the carnitas tacos since that's the only thing BOTH of us ate. The food seemed great, but it seems to be all about pushing the drinks for $$ and food safety was left to the sidelines."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2012-11-03 03:56:19', 'review_text': 'Great food. WOnderful atmosphere. Great Happy hour two for one Margaritas. I love the decor too. Beautiful Bar. Amazing flan!'}]}

{'name': 'Deep Sea Tasting Room', 'address': '217 G Stearns Wharf', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Venues & Event Spaces, Event Planning & Services, Wine Tasting Room, Arts & Entertainment, Food, Wine Bars, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Nightlife, Wineries', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-20:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-20:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-20:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-20:0', 'Friday': '11:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': True, 'lot': False, 'valet': True}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-18 00:53:58', 'review_text': "Beautiful beautiful view and friendly staff. We went on a rainy morning and still enjoyed the view. Wines are serviceable but it's really about the view."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-03 20:29:36', 'review_text': "It's a great location to have a drink. Beautiful views. Good breeze. It's unfortunate that the wine isn't as good as the location."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-01 23:32:42', 'review_text': 'Good Afternoon,

I am again submitting this review in reference to prior feedback i offered regarding an unfortunate very racially charged incident at Deep Sea Tasting room. To date the venue has still made no attempt at reaching out to me to discuss this rather u fortunate encounter with management that resulted in me cancelling my membership and not returning.

I wish the follow-up on the part of the leadership was as good as the view from the tasting room.'}]}

{'name': 'Campus Point Coffee', 'address': '6560 Pardall Rd', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Cafes, Coffee & Tea, Bakeries, Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-10 17:12:03', 'review_text': "A friend got me interested in this coffee shop when she mentioned they sell vegan cookies. I'm vegan, and it's actually rather tough to find vegan sweet snacks in IV, so I was excited to try Campus Point. Funnily enough, when I headed over for a studying session, they were sold out! Guess those cookies must be good. 

However, the coconut charcoal mocha I tried was delicious--and vegan! Staff were super friendly, and I appreciated the indoor and outdoor seating options. Also, there's a toilet, which is a bonus, and the empanadas looked really yummy. I'll have to try one next time I visit."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-08 22:10:42', 'review_text': 'Finally a place in Isla Vista with a bathroom!

Beyond the much needed bathroom this cafe offers a plethora of interesting drinks on top of providing all the basics. I got an iced charcoal mocha that was perfect to get rid of my mid afternoon slump.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-08 06:06:23', 'review_text': "This is such a cute lil coffee shop in the heart of IV. There's tables inside and outside to do work or chill, and sometimes there's an open mic outside. Prices are average for your local non-corporate coffee shop. The menu has a wide variety of drinks, and sometimes they post about BOGO's or 50% off on their instagram page. I'd definitely recommend this place to anyone who loves coffee and needs a place to study!"}]}

{'question': 'the difference between a poa and a durable power of attorney on a checking account', 'passages': 'passage 1:Durable Powers of Attorney. The best way to give someone authority over your financial matters is to sign a document called a “durable power of attorney for finances,” naming someone you trust as your “attorney-in-fact.” This gives the person the right to handle financial or property matters for you.

passage 2:(2) “Power of attorney account” means an account in the name of a natural person as principal and with respect to which one or more other natural persons have been designated as agents with the right to make deposits to and to withdraw funds from or draw checks on such account;

passage 3:Once the document is signed and notarized, you should give the original signed Power of Attorney document to the person you chose as your agent so she or he knows the limits of the powers given and can prove that fact to others, such as your bank.

'}

{'name': 'Via Vai Trattoria Pizzeria', 'address': '1483 E Valley Rd, Ste 20', 'city': 'Montecito', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Pizza, Restaurants, Italian', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:30-21:0', 'Tuesday': '11:30-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:30-21:0', 'Friday': '11:30-21:30', 'Saturday': '11:30-21:30', 'Sunday': '11:30-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-16 04:36:01', 'review_text': 'I understand that they are understaffed and the reasons.
We had lunch there last weekend Three of the four lunches were good. My lunch was inedible I ordered grilled Italian sausages with sautéed spinach and polenta. Only the spinach was edible No one came to see if we were happy with our meals.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-05 19:01:57', 'review_text': "The staff could not have been more welcoming on a stormy Santa Barbara evening. Everyone in our party of six was delighted by the food and ambience. This is one of Montecito's treasures!"}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-09-13 02:41:36', 'review_text': "Please do not go here ! Absolutely the worst Italian food I've had in years! Meatballs tasted frozen and undercooked. The fish had no flavor. The bread was stale. There was literally nothing that was good. Why they have any customers I honestly cannot say. Believe the other yelp reviews they really are that bad!!!

STAY AWAY"}]}

{'name': "Sam's To Go", 'address': '315 Meigs Rd, Ste I', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Sandwiches, Restaurants, American (New)', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-21:0', 'Friday': '10:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-19:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-03 00:05:08', 'review_text': "This was our first time at Sams and it was delicious!! Excellent customer service, they were so sweet. We got the #11 Italian cold cuts, and the veggie sandwich #29 both were so good! The bread was so fresh and you could tell the ingredients were really quality! My daughter got the turkey sandwich and she is the pickiest eater and she loved it! Can't wait to go back"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-10 03:34:00', 'review_text': "The couple who runs the place are so nice and funny, and the sandwiches are delicious. It doesn't look fancy, but do yourself a favor and try it out. The Pastrami Avocado and Cheese was delicious. Warning, the medium size sandwich is BIG."}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-28 21:43:45', 'review_text': 'I've been going to Sam's for the past several years while visiting beautiful Santa Barbara from the San Francisco Bay area. I've always enjoyed the sandwiches from Sam's. Unfortunately, my wife and I just finished eating their turkey sandwich and in all honesty, it' was just, Ok, more like disappointing...

We were disappointed because it appears the quality and taste of the sandwich has digressed to a "point of no return"... The sandwich was sloppily made, poorly wrapped, and importantly, the man behind the counter (usual guy) seems to have gotten cantankerous over time. He chastised me for not ordering both white and wheat bread sandwiches the way he wanted, getting perturbed for asking for olives in my sandwich and, he had a smart alec - bad attitude demeanor about him - poor customer service.

Suffice it to say, we will not be going back to Sam's. There are too many good delis in the Cliffs Dr. area to be subjected to poor quality sandwiches and an unpleasant customer experience...'}]}

{'name': "Basil's Italian", 'address': '608 Anacapa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Sandwiches, Delis, Pizza, Italian, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-21:0', 'Friday': '11:0-21:30', 'Saturday': '11:0-21:30', 'Sunday': '16:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': True, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2018-10-22 02:03:20', 'review_text': 'Went tonight to find the place closed  - looks like for good. Everything was gone but tables and chairs. Sad - it became our go to Italian place.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-10-06 03:20:21', 'review_text': "This place is amazing. If you want great authentic Italian and warm friendly service... this is where you need to be. It blows my mind more people don't know how good this place is. Top 3 Italian in town for sure: the complimentary bread is amazing. The wine... delicious and my tummy is never unhappy leaving here. JUST COME!! You will not regret it :) love you basil's!!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-09-28 21:22:14', 'review_text': 'Off the beaten path but well worth a visit!

Had lunch here today. The sweet server brought out some soft foccacia bread. Combo pizza was hot and loaded with fresh toppings. Egg plant parmesan was Panko breaded and topped with a rich tomato sauce with delicious pasta on the side. 

Shout out to Rosemary...thank you!'}]}

{'name': 'Nikka Ramen', 'address': '5701 Calle Real', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Japanese, Ramen', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '17:0-21:30', 'Wednesday': '17:0-21:30', 'Thursday': '17:0-21:30', 'Friday': '17:0-21:30', 'Saturday': '17:0-21:30', 'Sunday': '17:0-21:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': None, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': True, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-19 06:15:16', 'review_text': "Amazing place, great food , great location. The atmosphere was fun, the music was great. I can tell it's a very popular spot. Servers are very attentive. I will definitely go back again."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-18 01:53:38', 'review_text': "Officially my favorite ramen spot. We don't live in the area but now make it a point to stop by and satisfy our Nikka craving whenever we're in Goleta.

The gyoza was a yummy appetizer but the spicy tuna was sooooo goood! I could eat 10 of those! The basic pork tonkatsu was just as delicious as I remember. Al dente noodles and broth cooked to perfection. The pork chashu is A1 quality. Every ingredient was meant to be on that plate from the tender pork chunks to the salad to the soft boiled egg.

We love Nikka. Period."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-07 01:34:51', 'review_text': 'Holly F@ck... mind blowing. Literally spent the last 20 minutes of my life having a mouth gasm. My knees are weak, And ima little sweaty. This ramen just had its way with me.... and I liked it'}]}

{'name': "Giovanni's", 'address': '1187 Coast Village Rd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Pizza, Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2019-01-08 15:17:24', 'review_text': 'Delicious! I go once a week for the lunch special, slice (which is large) and a salad. Service is quick'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-12-02 22:16:29', 'review_text': 'The pizza here is so yummy!
Everyone who worked here was very friendly and accommodating. We got the lunch special and itnwas a good deal. Pizza crust was perfect, just the right thickness soft and chewy, while still holding up. Seasoned with oregano, just the right amount of sauce too.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2018-09-01 04:35:00', 'review_text': "Jesus Christ! Where's the customer service! I don't want to be treated like royalty but I at least want to be acknowledged by employees. If I wanted to be referred to as a fat ass I would have rather it be said to my face...


Ps food sucked."}]}

{'name': 'Peebee & Jays', 'address': '1007 Casitas Pass Rd', 'city': 'Carpinteria', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Sandwiches, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:30-16:0', 'Tuesday': '10:30-16:0', 'Wednesday': '10:30-16:0', 'Thursday': '10:30-16:0', 'Friday': '10:30-16:0', 'Saturday': '10:30-16:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': False, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-21 19:40:04', 'review_text': "Their sandwiches are fantastic, but don't opt for the cauliflower flatbread. They pack so much into these sandwiches that the flatbread can't handle it, so you're paying extra for a flimsier sandwich. I've also had trouble getting all my points for my weekly purchases. Their system is confusing, and they were unresponsive after multiple attempts to fix it. That said, their sandwiches are all great. Go for soft rolls with the Bacon Went on a Date and add turkey. So good."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-14 20:09:15', 'review_text': 'I got a lot pb with honey and a Nutella pb with marshmallow fluff they were pretty good the only real issue I had was that the crust was rubbery and hard to but into but over all it was super delicious'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-13 20:20:58', 'review_text': 'I will never go back to this location again. The workers in general have a negative attitude and think the customers owe them a medal for showing up to work. I placed a pick up order and put on the special instructions for the Mayo and Mustard to be on the side. Well, I got my sandwich and it was drenched in Mayo, something I wanted to avoid. I called them and the employee told me they could remake it. I threw the sandwich away and about 15 mins later got a call and was told that I had to bring the sandwich back. I told them I already tossed it in the garbage then the employee put his manager on the line and she was so RUDE and said that I need to bring it back ( I wasn't about to dig through the trash) and I said that the employee never said anything about bringing the sandwich back in the first conversation and he should have said something and expect me to still have it. And she said very unprofessionally, "well he didn't know." I told her that is a failure on the training and not the customer. She then said that next time I need to specifically write the word "everything" on the side instead of using commas as I did. This manager is absolutely disgusting and clearly has no basic customer service skills. 

This isn't the first time my pick up order has been destroyed. But the way that "manager" spoke to me and handledis why I will NEVER go there again and will tell all my coworkers to stay away. 

To the owner of this location: good Managers are hard to come by but you can absolutely do better then who was working on 10/13/21 @ 12:30 pm. She is horrible at her job and will continue to drive away customers with her terrible attitude.'}]}

{'name': 'Brasil Arts Cafe', 'address': '1230 State St, Ste C', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Juice Bars & Smoothies, Breakfast & Brunch, Brazilian, Restaurants, Food, Salad, Acai Bowls', 'hours': {'Monday': '17:0-20:30', 'Thursday': '17:0-20:30', 'Friday': '17:0-20:30', 'Saturday': '10:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-16:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-21 06:50:22', 'review_text': "Our hosts Roberta and Mestre Daniel Yoshimi (aka Prof. Chin) provided an excellent menu of the favorite foods of Brazil (o Brasil, em português). One who appreciates tasty-good food simply cannot stay away very long. My tri tip was delicious, and the multiple traditional sides were exactly on-point. (Prices are friendly too.)

I used to visit this establishment weekly to take part in great African drumming classes, and it's fun to revisit the festive atmosphere and food. They present their cuisine and culture with hospitality, nuance and great cooking skills.

#HighlyRecommended"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-18 05:28:16', 'review_text': 'my boyfriend and I went here for dinner and it was a nice experience :) we each got a caipirinha to drink which was good and my boyfriend LOVED the stroganoff! My Brazilian cesar was good and the brigadiero which we got to go was AMAZING! I would go back to try more! The lady told us to make ourselves at home which was a sweet sentiment!! The people were very nice :,)'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-15 12:06:28', 'review_text': 'The restaurant facility itself may not look all that elegant and appealing but the service and the food really blows that away. They serve food for each meal of the day but I personally would recommend going for breakfast and trying one of their acai fruit bowls. Slightly on the pricier side but so worth it and you will be healthily full for hours to come! The culture here is also something that is unique and interesting. Great place for family brunch!'}]}

{'name': "Mama's Bakery & Deli", 'address': '5342 Hollister Ave', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Food, Delis, Bakeries', 'hours': {'Monday': '6:0-16:30', 'Tuesday': '6:0-16:30', 'Wednesday': '6:0-16:30', 'Thursday': '6:0-16:30', 'Friday': '6:0-16:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': False, 'street': True, 'lot': True, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2017-04-14 17:12:21', 'review_text': "Solid Banh Mi sandwiches at a decent price. It's not San Francisco, but it will have to do.it work ld be nice if their bread was crispier and if they had lemongrass pork"}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2017-03-24 23:17:39', 'review_text': "Really hard to spot out, but I'm glad I found it! I would've never expected this to be a business that served pho and banh mi if I just drove by it, but I'm glad curiosity got the best of me and I'd like to try this place more often. 

I ordered half a pork banh mi with everything on it and it was reminiscent of the Vietnamese spots in the east bay suburbs. My only complaint is their bread isn't as flaky and it's more soft and dense, but it does the job for a craving. They didn't skimp out on the pork which is good. 

The lady running the counter was really nice and I got my sandwich way faster than I'd expect anywhere else in this area. Worth it!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2017-03-15 18:18:55', 'review_text': "Freshest sandwich in town. The bread is so soft and the ingredients are so fresh. Never greasy, light yet filling. So delicious! My favorite is the pastrami, it's the Wednesday special. If you like your sandwich with everything make sure you let them know or they won't put condiments on it. Must try!"}]}

