The new people behind the bar were nice, we were served in reasonable time, the bar was very quiet and it felt like as if it were just really slow business. Really sad actually, I had high hopes for this place."}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2012-06-25 23:55:16', 'review_text': 'This place is just okay. Ordered a scotch "neat" and the young bartender had no clue what I meant. I explained it, then he began to condescend to me that drinking that sounds nasty to him...scowling at me the entire time. Wow. Nice move to demean the customer!

It's fine to hang out with a group of friends, but don't get your hopes up. Pretty bland establishment in my opinion...and I love low-key. This is not low-key, it's no-key, if you get my drift.'}]}

{'name': 'The Blue Owl', 'address': '5 W Canon Perdido', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, American (New), Thai, Restaurants, Asian Fusion, Desserts, Cafes, Sandwiches, Caterers, Event Planning & Services', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '11:0-20:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-20:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-20:0', 'Friday': '11:0-2:30', 'Saturday': '11:0-2:30', 'Sunday': '11:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': True, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': None, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-19 05:49:47', 'review_text': 'I got a tofu banh mi, and it was pretty disappointing. The sandwich was fairly small for the price, and the inside of the sandwich was basically empty. Like, if you looked at it from the side, you would think it was just a piece of bread sliced down the middle. Seriously!

To add insult to injury, it tastes *nothing* like a banh mi. They should just call it something else because there was nothing inside that sandwich that tasted anything remotely like a banh mi does.

Three stars because my friend got a turkey sandwich that they really loved, so just averaging out the stars between the two of us.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 18:03:45', 'review_text': "This place slaps! I've lived in SB for 5 years and I hit Blue owls all the time. 10/10 would recommend. Fav is the Rice with pork and spicy chili sauce!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 00:35:57', 'review_text': 'What a great little lunch spot! We dropped by one afternoon and were really pleasantly surprised but the quality of the food. Reasonably priced as well, if you factor in the Santa Barbara "tax". The beet salad was really fresh and flavorful, and don't forget to throw an egg on top of that fried rice! Did I mention they serve beer? Not that you would ever have one during lunchtime...'}]}

{'name': 'Union Ale', 'address': '214 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, American (Traditional), Restaurants, Cocktail Bars, Nightlife', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-23:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-23:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-23:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-23:0', 'Friday': '11:0-23:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-23:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-23:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2016-09-23 22:32:27', 'review_text': "2nd transformation in 18 months...same owners, but now it feels like there's even less on the menu, and it's even more disorganized. What remains arrives without salad or fries or even a tidbit of  garnish. Your food comes on a metal tray without napkins or eating tools. If you order a hamburger, expect it to come under a super greasy bun. 

The patio is no longer covered so you'll be sitting in direct sunlight. It feels like this place is having an extended identity crisis. 

Damn if the funk zone doesn't need some decent dependable lunch places. This establishment is really missing out on an easy opportunity here. Great location, nice facility, but no thought or care in what they're serving up or in what they want to be."}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2016-01-10 02:25:11', 'review_text': "Horrible service. It took 20 minutes to get a drink order when it wasn't even that busy. Their food is goods"}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2016-01-04 20:55:40', 'review_text': "2 stars for the beer choices which is the only positive remnant of what was one of my go to places downtown. They've all but eliminated all the great food they served. They've now removed all but 2 TVs. Very disappointing business choices. I walked in this past weekend to catch a nationally televised hockey game, something I've done dozens of times here in the past. The bartender acknowledges us but is so busy covering the entire restaurant that he didn't get to us for nearly 10 minutes. We had to walk out and find a more suitable place to catch the game. Can't say I'll have a desire to go back. This town was already lacking decent sports bars with a good beer selection."}]}

