The bartenders were super great and it seemed like a place for locals. Not touristy which was great.'}]}

{'name': 'Pick Up Stix', 'address': '5701 Calle Real', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Chinese, Restaurants, Fast Food', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-13 20:44:58', 'review_text': "If it has to be fast-food Americanized Chinese, I won't even consider Panda Express. But Pick up Stix is the best you can get in under 5 minutes. While their portion sizes tend to be under-whelming, their ingredients and general tastiness is a good compromise to the pig slop served elsewhere. This particular location is usually pretty clean and generally has friendly staff.

If you are in a hurry, stop by Pick Up Stix for some decent food."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2010-02-22 17:55:02', 'review_text': "Went to this place for the first time the other day.  It's sooo good! For a place that cooks fast, it's way better than panda express!  

Shrimp fried rice and honey chicken was what I got...and you get your moneys worth! and then they have a dollar menu too, hahaha. They have egg rolls on it, wontons, edamame, dumplings!  The food is bomb!"}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2009-09-16 05:27:21', 'review_text': "Kung Pao Chicken w/ Fried Rice for Mom. Pad Thai Chicken & Shrimp for me. $16 dollars, no drinks. Why did I wander away from my normal order? The pad thai was...ehhhh so-so. Kung Pao was pretty good, Rice was gross. Took 15 mins to get the food and no one was in there. I've had it before when I would have given 4 stars. Won't be rushing back."}]}

{'name': 'Coast Restaurant & Bar', 'address': 'Canary Hotel, 31 W Carrillo St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Event Planning & Services, American (New), Party & Event Planning, American (Traditional)', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-22:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-22:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-22:0', 'Friday': '7:0-23:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-23:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': True, 'lot': True, 'valet': True}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': True, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2015-06-28 02:55:51', 'review_text': 'My wife and I went for a special evening out.  The lounge setting and ambience was wonderful and relaxing. The dinning room had subtle elegance.  The bread was warm and tasty, butternut squash soup and the romaine wedge salad was delicious. The service was outstanding. All was wonderful until the main course. The short  ribs tasted like pot roast and the New York steak was ok-needed salt.  We really wanted it to be great but the main dishes lacked flavor. Now for dessert... Butterscotch pudding and lemon cheesecake were excellent.  We really wanted to give 4 stars but 3 is all we can give it.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2013-03-20 03:27:00', 'review_text': "We were all very tired after a long day of work and being on the road, so we decided to try the restaurant in our hotel, which was conveniently located in our hotel's lobby.

We started our evening sharing the roasted California mussels seasoned perfectly and served with sourdough bread.  Then for our main course my daughter and I shared the savory manilla clams served over hand cut tagliatelle seasoned with basil, lemon and chile.  My husband ordered the crisy duck breast over potato gnocci and told both the waiter and I how he was in heaven that they had created a dish with two of his favorite meals put together in one.  We topped off the night with a bottle of Conundrum wine and a serving of their warm, comforting bread pudding and ice cream and called it a night!

The service was friendly and quick, and the food was delicious.  We will definitely be back the next time we're visiting the wonderful city of Santa Barbara!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2013-03-16 18:15:54', 'review_text': 'We decided to eat at Coast tonight because we wanted to try something different in Santa Barbara.  We ordered  the mussels, the pork belly sliders, shishito peppers and the pork ribs everything we had was really very good but the real stand out were the mussels the sauce was accompanied with a sourdough toast that was delicious.  Just before we left James Siao the head chef came out and talked to us we told him how he really enjoyed the meal.'}]}

{'name': 'Revolver', 'address': '1429 San Andres St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Pizza', 'hours': {'Wednesday': '16:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '16:0-22:0', 'Friday': '16:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '16:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '16:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'divey': True, 'hipster': None, 'casual': None, 'touristy': None, 'trendy': True, 'intimate': None, 'romantic': None, 'classy': None, 'upscale': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-06 20:15:13', 'review_text': "Nothing derails my good intentions of starting a diet like a Revolver Pizza craving! It's absolutely the BEST!! Beautifully handmade crust and fresh toppings. Not fancy just delicious. And the salads are incredible. Best Caesar with real anchovy dressing. Market salad has yummy dill ranch, shaved vegetables on yummy lettuce. I don't love the atmosphere, so we always get it to go. It's super popular so get your order in early! But it's definitely our favorite pizza in SB."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-01 06:13:46', 'review_text': 'Great pizza but limited toppings odd hours and long wait time for food.

They really should open at 11am like any other normal pizza place.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-20 02:58:37', 'review_text': "Hands down the best dang pizza in all of Santa Barbara. Not even close. Simple menu and from the crisp on the crust and bottom to the tang in the red sauce, SB you have a winner. It's artisan pizza meets NY on the west coast. Proves you don't need to be in the funk zone to have something great and feels like Brooklyn back 20
Years ago in the fact that they are hip but hard working and making something great. The Caesar salad had a great dressing and fresh greens to boot."}]}

{'name': 'Highway Karaoke and Fresh Tea', 'address': '7127 Hollister Ave, Ste 23, University Plaza Shopping Ctr', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Juice Bars & Smoothies, Bubble Tea, Nightlife, Karaoke, Food', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:30-23:30', 'Tuesday': '11:30-23:30', 'Wednesday': '11:30-23:30', 'Thursday': '11:30-23:30', 'Friday': '11:30-1:30', 'Saturday': '11:30-1:30', 'Sunday': '11:30-23:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': True, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2019-07-08 16:50:33', 'review_text': "Came here for boba a few times, and while it is pretty good the boba can also be unpredictable. I've gone a few times and the boba was perfectly cooked, and a few other times it was too soft. Still a great option for boba in SB!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-03-28 05:30:02', 'review_text': 'I enjoyed my time at this karaoke place last year either in September or October. I came to this place because I wanted to treat a friend out to some Asian style karaoke who lived in Central California. This place was the closest that I saw that was between Southern and Central California. The first time that I came there was by myself. I was the only one who used the karaoke room. I do not think that a lot of people know about this karaoke place. This place also sell boba tea drinks as well. I stayed at the place to almost closing. The worker there was very nice in that she did not try to rush me out of the room since I was the only one there.

The 2nd time that I went there was when I reserved the small room for 3 people. The female coworker, who could have been the owner, was very nice to give us the medium sized room with no additional charge. The private karaoke rooms were very cute with the Hello Kitty Decorations. The sound system was good and the English song choices were enough to keep my friends and I entertained. We could have been there for a few more hours if we were not charged by the hour.'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2019-03-04 20:59:03', 'review_text': "UPDATE: My friends and I were looking forward to going on a Friday night and we finally found a time that was suitable for all of us. Even after Yelp and google both told us they were open at 7pm on a Friday evening, they were closed with no explanation. We even tried calling but they seemed to hang up after I got through. We were really disappointed that we drove all the way there and met up and some of us even canceled previous plans to go to karaoke just to find out that they were closed.


This is usually our go-to place for karaoke in Santa Barbara because it's the only room-style karaoke but the drinks and milk tea are lacking. For karaoke it is a good place to go with a big group of friends and just rent out a room. The rooms are not completely sound proof but who cares when you're having fun with friends. The only downside would be that some songs are hard to find with their system and they don't have any korean or Japanese songs that we could find. Other than that, it's a pretty good place for karaoke."}]}

{'name': "Petrini's Restaurant", 'address': '5711 Calle Real', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'American (New), Italian, Restaurants, Pizza', 'hours': {'Monday': '16:30-21:0', 'Tuesday': '16:30-21:0', 'Wednesday': '16:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '16:30-21:0', 'Friday': '16:30-21:30', 'Saturday': '16:30-21:0', 'Sunday': '16:30-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-09-02 07:51:10', 'review_text': "I tend not to expect much from food locations in Strip Malls.  While staying in the Santa Barbara area, I just wanted a good piece of Pizza. We stopped here while on a walk and ordered an onion and cheese pizza, small size.  Neither of us could believe how fresh and great it was! The sauce was a good homemade red with Italian spices and fresh tomato flavor. Just enough good cheese.  We stopped in twice after having such great luck.  Tried the salads, pasta and more pizza, garlic bread and wine.  Family owned and run place that's cordial and homey.   This is the kind of place you find in Chicago and New York. Just a little gem with friendly people and really good Italian food!"}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2016-08-17 01:35:09', 'review_text': "Well, I tried eating at this Petrini's again, and I'm really sad to report that the food has gotten worse AND more expensive. The Chicken Picatta was drowning in butter, or grease; I'm not sure what that was. The fettuccine Alfredo that came with it was undercooked and had zero taste. We also were served garlic bread that was burned to black. To make things worse, I took the food home because I just could eat it at the restaurant. I was hungry later so I ate it. 
Oh My God.....I couldn't keep it down. I got such a stomach ache from that food. Petrini's , you are a local restaurant and I really try to support local businesses, but you are bad for my health."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2016-07-11 15:51:04', 'review_text': 'I have not been in here for many years, but we stopped in the other night and it was tasty traditional american italian food for a great price. The meat raviolis were very tender and delicious and the sauce was spot on. The spaghetti and meatballs (the yard stick for any italian review) were also very good. I also really enjoyed my cup of minestrone soup, really hit the spot. The waiters were very attentive and the place had a very welcoming and tidy atmosphere. 

The only downside, the water tasted horrible, I think they need to replace their filter or something.'}]}

{'name': 'Piranha Restaurant & Sushi Bar', 'address': '714 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Sushi Bars', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2008-08-08 19:51:46', 'review_text': 'The sushi was mediocre but I still like the environment and the service!'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2008-07-26 05:03:21', 'review_text': '"after a lovely day at the beach, my husband and i decided to finish off the day with some sushi. we'd eaten at piranha before and enjoyed it, but after tonight's experience, i can safely say we will never return. it wasn't heinous--but for 80$, the quality of the food and service was pretty abysmal. not only was the sushi NOT super fresh and tasty, especially as compared to katsuya in encino, but the waitstaff was inattentive (we had to call out for the hostess finally to get our waitress's attention), the waitress made a mistake on our order and did not recitfy it (she brought out sea urchin instead of eel--when we brought it to her attention, she did not remove the unwanted, uneaten item from our bill), AND there was a long hair in one of our rolls! At most sushi establishments, they bring out the items as they are prepared, but here, we had to wait a fairly long time before  being served, and then it was everything, all at once.  Plus, i really like it when the meal commences with a nice, warm hand towel and some complimentary edaname--typical of most sushi places, but NOT here. Overall, a very unpleasant, unappetizing, unsatisfying gastronomical experience!"'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2008-06-02 15:01:40', 'review_text': "This is a nice place to sit outside on State St.  I was a tad bit early for sushi (they don't start making sushi until 5:30), so I decided on their Warm Spinach Salad instead.  It was deeeelish.  I had a blackberry martini to sip on, which was also really good.  The server was really nice and attentive the entire time.  

I've also been here previously and have sat in their outside area upstairs, which is also nice.  

I'm curious to try their sushi soon, which might alter my rating."}]}

{'name': 'Char West', 'address': '221 Stearns Wharf', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Fish & Chips, Food, Seafood, American (Traditional), Fast Food, Coffee & Tea, Breakfast & Brunch', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-17:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-17:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-17:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-17:0', 'Friday': '7:0-17:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-19:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-19:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': True, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': False, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': True, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-26 04:52:35', 'review_text': "It was the worst fish n chips I've ever had. I believe the fish was tilapia as it tasted muddy. We felt disgusted after eating there. The same type of fish was used in the fish taco. We were hungry and was super disappointed with the meal. If you want to eat muddy tasty fish, you can give it a try. It's worst than the frozen fish from the grocery store."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-09 18:16:50', 'review_text': "Nice stop on the pier for coffee

